<title>RUSSIA: Russian 364-day T-bill yields 31.08 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 364-day T-bill yields 31.08 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 31.08 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in the 30.61-31.58 percent range.</p>
<p>The 23005 issue, maturing on April 22, 1998, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed on Tuesday at 77.31 to yield 30.52 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		 23006</p>
<p>    Issue volume		  7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		 1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		8.89 trln</p>
<p>    Sold			    6.84 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			5.22 trln</p>
<p>    Average price		 76.34 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price     76.11 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		 31.08 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield    31.48 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			   364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		 May 6, 1998</p>
<p>On May 7 the Finance Ministry will offer four trillion roubles in 161-day Treasury bills (series 22082).</p>
<p>It will also repay about 7.25 trillion roubles in maturing issue of 140-day T-bills (series 22063) and pay 468.64 billion roubles in interest on the series 24006 OFZ interest-bearing bond.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
